.TH PLUGIN-QUALIFICATION-DB 1 2026-11-19 plugin-db-qualification "User Commands"
.SH NAME
plugin-qualification-db \- query the OpenMixer qualification store
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B plugin-qualification-db query
.RB [ \-\-sha256
.IR hash ]
.RB [ \-\-format
.IR format ]
.RB [ \-\-uri
.IR uri ]
.RB [ \-\-offer
.IR offer ]
.RB [ \-\-host\-class
.IR class ]
.RB [ \-\-rate
.IR n ]
.RB [ \-\-quantum
.IR n ]
.RB [ \-\-pkg\-format
.IR f ]
.RB [ \-\-pkg\-name
.IR n ]
.RB [ \-\-pkg\-version
.IR v ]
.RB [ \-\-pkg\-release
.IR r ]
.RB [ \-\-pkg\-distro
.IR d ]
.RB [ \-\-pkg\-arch
.IR a ]
.B \-\-json
.RI [ common\ options ]
.br
.B plugin-qualification-db check
.RI [ common\ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads the qualification store with libplugin-qualification-db: the base database installed by
plugin-qualification-records and the user layer, merged by whole record (a user record shadows every base
record of its plugin, offer and host class). The command is the reader for programs that cannot link the library.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B query \-\-json
Prints one JSON object per line for every result the filters match, user layer first: the layer, the plugin key,
the offer, the host class, the set, the package fields (null when not known), the cell's rate, quantum and outcome,
the cost, latency and memory figures with their has_ flags, and every verdict of the record. Words and numbers only.
.TP
.B check
Opens both layers and checks every word column against the installed contract domains. Prints
.B ok
and exits 0, or prints the refusal code and its message and exits 1.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-base " path"
The base database. Default: the value of
.BR PLUGIN_QUALIFICATION_DB_BASE ,
else /usr/share/omx/qualification/qualification.sqlite.
.TP
.BI \-\-user " path"
The user layer; an empty path reads none. Default: the value of
.BR PLUGIN_QUALIFICATION_DB_USER ,
else the layer under the home directory of the effective user,
.IR ~/.local/share/omx/qualification/qualification.sqlite .
An absent user layer is an empty layer.
.TP
.BI \-\-contract\-dir " dir"
The contract directory the word check reads. Default: the value of
.BR OMX_CONTRACT_PATH ,
else the installed contract directory.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.BR PLUGIN_QUALIFICATION_DB_BASE ,
.BR PLUGIN_QUALIFICATION_DB_USER
and
.BR OMX_CONTRACT_PATH
are read by this command only, and a flag beats its variable. The library reads no environment variable.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 when the store is refused (the code is
.B qualification-db.absent ,
.BR qualification-db.unreadable ,
.BR qualification-db.not-a-store ,
.BR qualification-db.schema-mismatch ,
.BR qualification-db.schema-other ,
.BR qualification-db.domain-too-old ,
.BR qualification-db.word-unknown ,
.BR qualification-db.hot-journal ,
.B qualification-db.busy
or a code of the contract loader); 2 on a usage error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/omx/qualification/qualification.sqlite
The base database.
.TP
.I /usr/share/plugin-qualification-db/qualification.sql
The DDL of the store (the schema variable of plugin-qualification-db.pc).
